[{:db/id 17592186175957 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fbdb7241-60ea-5f22-afcd-5e46de779c9a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fbdb7241-60ea-5f22-afcd-5e46de779c9a" :question/id #uuid "fbdb7241-60ea-5f22-afcd-5e46de779c9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-353482" :question/problem "The subscriber count $P(t)$ of a streaming service follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=2P(5\\,000-P),\\,P(0)=300.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the subscriber count growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](images/90/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFrom our equation, we see that $a=5000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $5000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5000=2500.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dbb704d4-511c-5244-871d-d498a47768aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbb704d4-511c-5244-871d-d498a47768aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbb704d4-511c-5244-871d-d498a47768aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e33b7888-14e2-559e-bca1-077f0916190c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e33b7888-14e2-559e-bca1-077f0916190c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e33b7888-14e2-559e-bca1-077f0916190c" :answer/id #uuid "e33b7888-14e2-559e-bca1-077f0916190c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092373 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8023cebc-048b-5288-9c32-1da095db126f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8023cebc-048b-5288-9c32-1da095db126f" :question/id #uuid "8023cebc-048b-5288-9c32-1da095db126f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103827" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\theta +{e}^{\\theta }$ for $-\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\theta +{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=1+{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(\\theta +{e}^{\\theta })^{2}+(1+{e}^{\\theta })^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta {e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }+1+2{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2{e}^{\\theta }(\\theta +1)+2{e}^{2\\theta }+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17a97da4-f06a-512c-b0f2-d273f0e4876b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17a97da4-f06a-512c-b0f2-d273f0e4876b" :answer-field/id #uuid "17a97da4-f06a-512c-b0f2-d273f0e4876b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c4d84b89-ed7c-5866-bbe7-886aa45f00d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fceb4866-634d-53f1-b923-46c9e70b07f5" "answer-c4d84b89-ed7c-5866-bbe7-886aa45f00d5" "answer-19a8a941-abee-5eec-a85d-2c36090c0c9e" "answer-c107c606-2649-543d-89fe-4a7928489ec5" "answer-829b49d5-b322-53c3-b0f4-1c6304fa46ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fceb4866-634d-53f1-b923-46c9e70b07f5" :answer/id #uuid "fceb4866-634d-53f1-b923-46c9e70b07f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta {e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4d84b89-ed7c-5866-bbe7-886aa45f00d5" :answer/id #uuid "c4d84b89-ed7c-5866-bbe7-886aa45f00d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2{e}^{\\theta }(\\theta +1)+2{e}^{2\\theta }+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19a8a941-abee-5eec-a85d-2c36090c0c9e" :answer/id #uuid "19a8a941-abee-5eec-a85d-2c36090c0c9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2{e}^{\\theta }(\\theta +1)+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c107c606-2649-543d-89fe-4a7928489ec5" :answer/id #uuid "c107c606-2649-543d-89fe-4a7928489ec5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}-2{e}^{\\theta }(1-\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-829b49d5-b322-53c3-b0f4-1c6304fa46ac" :answer/id #uuid "829b49d5-b322-53c3-b0f4-1c6304fa46ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}-2{e}^{\\theta }-2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083325 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b642f61b-90d3-52e8-a698-ed0e6fdd52ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b642f61b-90d3-52e8-a698-ed0e6fdd52ac" :question/id #uuid "b642f61b-90d3-52e8-a698-ed0e6fdd52ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-132849" :question/problem "In a factory, the average amount of sugar in a cookie is $15$ grams. However, $10%$ of cookies contain no more than $14$ grams of sugar. Assuming that the amount of sugar in each cookie is normally distributed, find the standard deviation of the amount of sugar in a cookie, rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.10\\,$ | $\\,0.15\\,$ | $\\,0.20\\,$ | $\\,0.25\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-2.3263\\,$ | $\\,-1.8808\\,$ | $\\,-1.6449\\,$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the amount (in grams) of sugar in a cookie. Then we have $X∼N(15,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ and we want to find the standard deviation $\\sigma .$ \n\nWe know that $P(X\\le 14)=0.10.$ Converting $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 14) & =0.10 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{14-15}{\\sigma }) & =0.10 \\\\ Φ(-\\frac{1}{\\sigma }) & =0.10 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.10).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{Φ}^{-1}(0.10)=-1.2816.\n$$\n\nFinally then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sigma } & =-1.2816 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sigma } & =1.2816 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{1}{1.2816} \\\\  & ≈0.78.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c889ce98-c36c-5100-9ccc-2833887780d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c889ce98-c36c-5100-9ccc-2833887780d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "c889ce98-c36c-5100-9ccc-2833887780d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3208f809-5202-519c-a4c1-b2c071b30e1b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70486f57-d8c6-5d88-9e76-73287f23fb7a" "answer-3208f809-5202-519c-a4c1-b2c071b30e1b" "answer-b360a2fc-6825-56f7-a4ae-202963cd606a" "answer-3633d1c4-a4bd-5d6c-9a1e-fe155268f04d" "answer-bf33ba30-f07a-5c5e-8673-051f5a7fed51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70486f57-d8c6-5d88-9e76-73287f23fb7a" :answer/id #uuid "70486f57-d8c6-5d88-9e76-73287f23fb7a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.75$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3208f809-5202-519c-a4c1-b2c071b30e1b" :answer/id #uuid "3208f809-5202-519c-a4c1-b2c071b30e1b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.78$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b360a2fc-6825-56f7-a4ae-202963cd606a" :answer/id #uuid "b360a2fc-6825-56f7-a4ae-202963cd606a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.8$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3633d1c4-a4bd-5d6c-9a1e-fe155268f04d" :answer/id #uuid "3633d1c4-a4bd-5d6c-9a1e-fe155268f04d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.82$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf33ba30-f07a-5c5e-8673-051f5a7fed51" :answer/id #uuid "bf33ba30-f07a-5c5e-8673-051f5a7fed51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.85$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-827107a2-7f92-5ca4-afee-8faa39aca13d" :activity/id #uuid "827107a2-7f92-5ca4-afee-8faa39aca13d" :activity/title "Quiz 4" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046645 :activity/steps ["step-576a51b8-08b4-57e9-9da7-c6ba4b57ef63" "step-284b50fd-d719-5102-8733-5376d2d513e4" "step-a48aca1d-b9af-5eb7-9522-d31ba40b69ea" "step-6ce11fb7-1ed0-50ca-8962-d9ee890ba212" "step-ba6e4c6c-2798-534e-907b-4117098421dc"] :activity/first-step "step-576a51b8-08b4-57e9-9da7-c6ba4b57ef63" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-576a51b8-08b4-57e9-9da7-c6ba4b57ef63" :step/id #uuid "576a51b8-08b4-57e9-9da7-c6ba4b57ef63" :step/content 17592186317515 :step/next "step-284b50fd-d719-5102-8733-5376d2d513e4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-284b50fd-d719-5102-8733-5376d2d513e4" :step/id #uuid "284b50fd-d719-5102-8733-5376d2d513e4" :step/content 17592186547038 :step/next "step-a48aca1d-b9af-5eb7-9522-d31ba40b69ea" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a48aca1d-b9af-5eb7-9522-d31ba40b69ea" :step/id #uuid "a48aca1d-b9af-5eb7-9522-d31ba40b69ea" :step/content "question-fbdb7241-60ea-5f22-afcd-5e46de779c9a" :step/next "step-6ce11fb7-1ed0-50ca-8962-d9ee890ba212" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6ce11fb7-1ed0-50ca-8962-d9ee890ba212" :step/id #uuid "6ce11fb7-1ed0-50ca-8962-d9ee890ba212" :step/content "question-8023cebc-048b-5288-9c32-1da095db126f" :step/next "step-ba6e4c6c-2798-534e-907b-4117098421dc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ba6e4c6c-2798-534e-907b-4117098421dc" :step/id #uuid "ba6e4c6c-2798-534e-907b-4117098421dc" :step/content "question-b642f61b-90d3-52e8-a698-ed0e6fdd52ac" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186052749 :answer-field/choices 17592186052752] [:db/retract 17592186052749 :answer-field/choices 17592186052754] [:db/retract 17592186052749 :answer-field/choices 17592186052750] [:db/retract 17592186052749 :answer-field/choices 17592186052751] {:db/id 17592186054798 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1938b4fe-a4da-5df4-945e-a4ba43cb2798" "question-e49f42fb-4ed5-5c34-8e9e-f41f753d3cfd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1938b4fe-a4da-5df4-945e-a4ba43cb2798" :question/id #uuid "1938b4fe-a4da-5df4-945e-a4ba43cb2798" :question/math-academy-id "q-39686" :question/problem "Solve $\\sqrt{-3x-8}=x+2.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the equation $\\sqrt{-3x-8}=x+2,$ we raise both sides to the power of $2.$  This allows us to get rid of the radical, and gives us a quadratic equation that is easier to solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{-3x-8} & =x+2 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{-3x-8})}^{2} & =(x+2)^{2} \\\\ -3x-8 & ={x}^{2}+4x+4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+7x+12 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x)+(3x+12) & =0 \\\\ x(x+4)+3(x+4) & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x+4) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemember that in square root equations, we should always check the obtained value(s) to ensure that they are actually solutions of the original equation.\n\n- First, we check whether the obtained value $x=-4$ is a solution of the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{-3(-4)-8} & \\overset{?}{=}-4+2 \\\\ \\sqrt{4} & \\overset{?}{=}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\ne -2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe value $x=-4$ does *not* satisfy the original equation, so we discard it.\n\n- Second, we check whether the obtained value $x=-3$ is a solution of the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{-3(-3)-8} & \\overset{?}{=}-3+2 \\\\ \\sqrt{1} & \\overset{?}{=}-1 \\\\ 1 & \\ne -1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe value $x=-3$ does *not* satisfy the original equation, so we discard it.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to $\\sqrt{-3x-8}=x+2x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3de2b104-d32f-5800-a490-24878cd6ff1e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3de2b104-d32f-5800-a490-24878cd6ff1e" :answer-field/id #uuid "3de2b104-d32f-5800-a490-24878cd6ff1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6ad116cc-f346-5585-9c55-b508e61fb4e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59872150-fbec-5d48-9fe6-1b9b9e554ed6" "answer-7e01fe28-888e-5714-9470-03041ce8461b" "answer-2de55bb9-4e8d-5f06-b11e-556b8e8249ed" "answer-36d4014c-9f06-558b-b2b4-ea6a2f47a4db" "answer-6ad116cc-f346-5585-9c55-b508e61fb4e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59872150-fbec-5d48-9fe6-1b9b9e554ed6" :answer/id #uuid "59872150-fbec-5d48-9fe6-1b9b9e554ed6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3,\\,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e01fe28-888e-5714-9470-03041ce8461b" :answer/id #uuid "7e01fe28-888e-5714-9470-03041ce8461b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,\\,-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2de55bb9-4e8d-5f06-b11e-556b8e8249ed" :answer/id #uuid "2de55bb9-4e8d-5f06-b11e-556b8e8249ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,\\,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36d4014c-9f06-558b-b2b4-ea6a2f47a4db" :answer/id #uuid "36d4014c-9f06-558b-b2b4-ea6a2f47a4db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3,\\,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ad116cc-f346-5585-9c55-b508e61fb4e6" :answer/id #uuid "6ad116cc-f346-5585-9c55-b508e61fb4e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The equation has no solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e49f42fb-4ed5-5c34-8e9e-f41f753d3cfd" :question/id #uuid "e49f42fb-4ed5-5c34-8e9e-f41f753d3cfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-39754" :question/problem "Solve $\\sqrt{5x-9}=x-1.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the equation $\\sqrt{5x-9}=x-1,$ we raise both sides to the power of $2.$  This allows us to get rid of the radical, and gives us a quadratic equation that is easier to solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5x-9} & =x-1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{5x-9})}^{2} & =(x-1)^{2} \\\\ 5x-9 & ={x}^{2}-2x+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+10 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+(-5x+10) & =0 \\\\ x(x-2)-5(x-2) & =0 \\\\ (x-5)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =2,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemember that in square root equations, we should always check the obtained value(s) to ensure that they are actually solutions of the original equation.\n\n- First, we check whether the obtained value $x=2$ is a solution of the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5(2)-9} & \\overset{?}{=}2-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{1} & \\overset{?}{=}1 \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIndeed, the value $x=2$ does satisfy the original equation.\n\n- Second, we check whether the obtained value $x=5$ is a solution of the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5(5)-9} & \\overset{?}{=}5-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{16} & \\overset{?}{=}4 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIndeed, the value $x=5$ does satisfy the original equation.\n\nTherefore, the solutions of $\\sqrt{5x-9}=x-1$  are $x=2,\\,5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d572b8ad-f569-5f9c-bd00-4b949d1c4e59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d572b8ad-f569-5f9c-bd00-4b949d1c4e59" :answer-field/id #uuid "d572b8ad-f569-5f9c-bd00-4b949d1c4e59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a89eae67-e29c-52cf-a4df-72219d50f3d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8376cf8b-1e0a-59fe-afd5-0011348cb1b6" "answer-11994bd3-02cd-5d54-9e80-6bf4d1f9a271" "answer-518703a7-6d82-5deb-9823-04f8892b81fa" "answer-b80abb0f-80c8-5d96-a7c3-66cc53eb5542" "answer-a89eae67-e29c-52cf-a4df-72219d50f3d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8376cf8b-1e0a-59fe-afd5-0011348cb1b6" :answer/id #uuid "8376cf8b-1e0a-59fe-afd5-0011348cb1b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11994bd3-02cd-5d54-9e80-6bf4d1f9a271" :answer/id #uuid "11994bd3-02cd-5d54-9e80-6bf4d1f9a271" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-518703a7-6d82-5deb-9823-04f8892b81fa" :answer/id #uuid "518703a7-6d82-5deb-9823-04f8892b81fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b80abb0f-80c8-5d96-a7c3-66cc53eb5542" :answer/id #uuid "b80abb0f-80c8-5d96-a7c3-66cc53eb5542" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a89eae67-e29c-52cf-a4df-72219d50f3d9" :answer/id #uuid "a89eae67-e29c-52cf-a4df-72219d50f3d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2,\\,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055252 :question/problem "Solve $\\sqrt{2-3x}=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Squaring both sides of the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2-3x} & =2 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{2-3x})}^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ 2-3x & =4 \\\\ 3x & =-2 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check the result by plugging it into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2-3(-\\frac{2}{3})} & \\overset{?}{=}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2-\\cancel{3}(-\\frac{2}{\\cancel{3}})} & \\overset{?}{=}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2-(-2)} & \\overset{?}{=}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2+2} & \\overset{?}{=}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{4} & \\overset{?}{=}2 \\\\ 2 & =2\\,\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe value $x=-\\frac{2}{3}$ satisfies the original equation, so we can accept it as a solution.\n\nTherefore, the solution to $\\sqrt{2-3x}=2$  is $x=-\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186052749 :answer-field/correct "answer-a8fb8a27-2cb4-5bca-b2c7-af9e02db982d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ef944fe-b546-5c3c-bb66-e324e8c66a3c" "answer-8610145b-97d5-54e0-93c8-3885eba86069" "answer-a8fb8a27-2cb4-5bca-b2c7-af9e02db982d" "answer-9b5ca04f-34a5-587c-b744-86213c713a80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ef944fe-b546-5c3c-bb66-e324e8c66a3c" :answer/id #uuid "0ef944fe-b546-5c3c-bb66-e324e8c66a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8610145b-97d5-54e0-93c8-3885eba86069" :answer/id #uuid "8610145b-97d5-54e0-93c8-3885eba86069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8fb8a27-2cb4-5bca-b2c7-af9e02db982d" :answer/id #uuid "a8fb8a27-2cb4-5bca-b2c7-af9e02db982d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b5ca04f-34a5-587c-b744-86213c713a80" :answer/id #uuid "9b5ca04f-34a5-587c-b744-86213c713a80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5c07c81a-6299-5f56-a72a-da105bc2e7c6" :activity/id #uuid "5c07c81a-6299-5f56-a72a-da105bc2e7c6" :activity/title "Solving Radical Equations" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048784 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-493c7f13-e45f-5f7f-bf76-16d264e435c3" "step-701496b1-5d28-5293-9b1c-d814d6e67a7b" "step-99997799-e2eb-5bf3-a5f0-77dab9e1f445"] :activity/first-step "step-493c7f13-e45f-5f7f-bf76-16d264e435c3" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-493c7f13-e45f-5f7f-bf76-16d264e435c3" :step/id #uuid "493c7f13-e45f-5f7f-bf76-16d264e435c3" :step/content "question-1938b4fe-a4da-5df4-945e-a4ba43cb2798" :step/next "step-701496b1-5d28-5293-9b1c-d814d6e67a7b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-701496b1-5d28-5293-9b1c-d814d6e67a7b" :step/id #uuid "701496b1-5d28-5293-9b1c-d814d6e67a7b" :step/content "question-e49f42fb-4ed5-5c34-8e9e-f41f753d3cfd" :step/next "step-99997799-e2eb-5bf3-a5f0-77dab9e1f445" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-99997799-e2eb-5bf3-a5f0-77dab9e1f445" :step/id #uuid "99997799-e2eb-5bf3-a5f0-77dab9e1f445" :step/content 17592186055252 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124654 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-698b79dc-de1f-5472-8b54-18da46bc32a4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-698b79dc-de1f-5472-8b54-18da46bc32a4" :question/id #uuid "698b79dc-de1f-5472-8b54-18da46bc32a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-37453" :question/problem "The function \n$f(x,y)$\nhas the first derivative\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2} & y{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(0,0).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $H(0,0)<0$\n\nII. $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(0,0)>0$\n\nIII. The point $(0,0)$ is a local minimum of $f$" :question/worked-solution "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nFirst, we notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2} & y{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2}\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=y\\text{ }\\,{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2})=(1+{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2})=(1+{y}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\text{ }\\,{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2})=xy\\text{ }\\,{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}(1+{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2} & xy\\text{ }\\,{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2} \\\\ xy\\text{ }\\,{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2} & (1+{y}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})/2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,0),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(0,0),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(0,0)=det({f}^{″}(0,0))={1}^{2}-{0}^{2}=1>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(0,0)=({f}^{″}(0,0))_{11}=1>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $H(0,0)>0$ and $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(0,0)>0,$ the point $(0,0)$ is a local minimum by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9878ae59-6ea6-5926-9207-b1e7edaba613"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9878ae59-6ea6-5926-9207-b1e7edaba613" :answer-field/id #uuid "9878ae59-6ea6-5926-9207-b1e7edaba613" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-63625bc2-1789-5d35-971e-846b92df64bf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc8a379b-a69d-592e-8528-13b53b904286" "answer-4cebeea4-ba06-5e53-be43-f6d3b1163a34" "answer-41f6b037-a592-5081-aab8-180757dfb407" "answer-63625bc2-1789-5d35-971e-846b92df64bf" "answer-acc4f7de-f63c-51cd-b58d-6560706da8f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc8a379b-a69d-592e-8528-13b53b904286" :answer/id #uuid "fc8a379b-a69d-592e-8528-13b53b904286" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4cebeea4-ba06-5e53-be43-f6d3b1163a34" :answer/id #uuid "4cebeea4-ba06-5e53-be43-f6d3b1163a34" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41f6b037-a592-5081-aab8-180757dfb407" :answer/id #uuid "41f6b037-a592-5081-aab8-180757dfb407" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63625bc2-1789-5d35-971e-846b92df64bf" :answer/id #uuid "63625bc2-1789-5d35-971e-846b92df64bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acc4f7de-f63c-51cd-b58d-6560706da8f9" :answer/id #uuid "acc4f7de-f63c-51cd-b58d-6560706da8f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-bd9a456c-0340-58fa-a164-d6125ac2b9fb" :activity/id #uuid "bd9a456c-0340-58fa-a164-d6125ac2b9fb" :activity/title "The Second Partial Derivatives Test" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051048 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-828c9822-48e9-5c25-a3de-311af96cc1b0" "step-bd1cf028-18c6-5036-a2eb-18834a5e4c1c" "step-59c32226-9848-5c7f-b446-707c5e49e63b" "step-bec870e8-b940-58ab-a1e0-8e41adc74bbe" "step-c3d9a002-9928-57fd-89bf-59d24c34b057"] :activity/first-step "step-828c9822-48e9-5c25-a3de-311af96cc1b0" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-828c9822-48e9-5c25-a3de-311af96cc1b0" :step/id #uuid "828c9822-48e9-5c25-a3de-311af96cc1b0" :step/content "question-698b79dc-de1f-5472-8b54-18da46bc32a4" :step/next "step-bd1cf028-18c6-5036-a2eb-18834a5e4c1c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bd1cf028-18c6-5036-a2eb-18834a5e4c1c" :step/id #uuid "bd1cf028-18c6-5036-a2eb-18834a5e4c1c" :step/content 17592186351244 :step/next "step-59c32226-9848-5c7f-b446-707c5e49e63b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-59c32226-9848-5c7f-b446-707c5e49e63b" :step/id #uuid "59c32226-9848-5c7f-b446-707c5e49e63b" :step/content 17592186534985 :step/next "step-bec870e8-b940-58ab-a1e0-8e41adc74bbe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bec870e8-b940-58ab-a1e0-8e41adc74bbe" :step/id #uuid "bec870e8-b940-58ab-a1e0-8e41adc74bbe" :step/content 17592186399468 :step/next "step-c3d9a002-9928-57fd-89bf-59d24c34b057" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c3d9a002-9928-57fd-89bf-59d24c34b057" :step/id #uuid "c3d9a002-9928-57fd-89bf-59d24c34b057" :step/content 17592186241041 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186099361 :answer-field/choices 17592186099362] [:db/retract 17592186099361 :answer-field/choices 17592186099363] [:db/retract 17592186099361 :answer-field/choices 17592186099364] [:db/retract 17592186099361 :answer-field/choices 17592186099365] [:db/retract 17592186099361 :answer-field/choices 17592186099366] {:db/id 17592186100987 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-370ca68a-a4c7-585b-aa83-7cfb70ebc27e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101361 :question/problem "The point $P$ with coordinates $(8,12)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=2f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $y=2f(x)$ represents a stretch of the function $y=f(x)$ by a factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $2.$\n\nTherefore, the point $(8,12)$ on $f(x)$ is mapped to the point $(8,2\\cdot 12)=(8,24),$ and this point must lie on the graph of $y=2f(x).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186099361 :answer-field/correct "answer-2d45c5ae-1977-58ce-b66c-6465eb267d0c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-538243a7-2282-5f10-a989-6f2e0978aa9c" "answer-297b5739-965f-5d97-afde-d24a71c50915" "answer-1d5c5df4-40c2-50ae-85fb-430c28173d99" "answer-2d45c5ae-1977-58ce-b66c-6465eb267d0c" "answer-b1ca4171-8d99-55e2-ab66-dae2712d819c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-538243a7-2282-5f10-a989-6f2e0978aa9c" :answer/id #uuid "538243a7-2282-5f10-a989-6f2e0978aa9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(16,12)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-297b5739-965f-5d97-afde-d24a71c50915" :answer/id #uuid "297b5739-965f-5d97-afde-d24a71c50915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(16,24)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d5c5df4-40c2-50ae-85fb-430c28173d99" :answer/id #uuid "1d5c5df4-40c2-50ae-85fb-430c28173d99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(8,12)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d45c5ae-1977-58ce-b66c-6465eb267d0c" :answer/id #uuid "2d45c5ae-1977-58ce-b66c-6465eb267d0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(8,24)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1ca4171-8d99-55e2-ab66-dae2712d819c" :answer/id #uuid "b1ca4171-8d99-55e2-ab66-dae2712d819c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(8,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-370ca68a-a4c7-585b-aa83-7cfb70ebc27e" :question/id #uuid "370ca68a-a4c7-585b-aa83-7cfb70ebc27e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81958" :question/problem "The point $P$ with coordinates $(10,8)$ lies on the curve $y=2f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $y=2f(x)$ represents a stretch of the function $y=f(x)$ by a factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $2.$\n\nThe point $Q(10,q)$ on $f(x)$ is mapped to the point $P(10,8)$ on $y=2f(x).$ Since we know that the $y$-coordinate of $P$ is $2$ times the $y$-coordinate of $Q,$ we can form the following equation:\n\n$$\n2q=8\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get $q=4.$ Therefore, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(10,4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4efac58-0e1b-5cda-b9ed-a1fe7c4d15f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4efac58-0e1b-5cda-b9ed-a1fe7c4d15f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4efac58-0e1b-5cda-b9ed-a1fe7c4d15f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-493c1ac4-f93b-5cc1-b151-9391c7ffa2b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-935c105d-8186-59e8-9c38-2769ba4d5f69" "answer-493c1ac4-f93b-5cc1-b151-9391c7ffa2b6" "answer-cd72122e-035b-5d73-a118-62046f1b574d" "answer-0e4ff37e-6e33-5e71-a809-34b53b71daa2" "answer-3bb4b77c-886c-5116-b814-fa3023c988a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-935c105d-8186-59e8-9c38-2769ba4d5f69" :answer/id #uuid "935c105d-8186-59e8-9c38-2769ba4d5f69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(10,16)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-493c1ac4-f93b-5cc1-b151-9391c7ffa2b6" :answer/id #uuid "493c1ac4-f93b-5cc1-b151-9391c7ffa2b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(10,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd72122e-035b-5d73-a118-62046f1b574d" :answer/id #uuid "cd72122e-035b-5d73-a118-62046f1b574d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(20,16)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e4ff37e-6e33-5e71-a809-34b53b71daa2" :answer/id #uuid "0e4ff37e-6e33-5e71-a809-34b53b71daa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bb4b77c-886c-5116-b814-fa3023c988a7" :answer/id #uuid "3bb4b77c-886c-5116-b814-fa3023c988a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100986 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-46986aeb-b3ed-5a20-9bf3-78659d9de421"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-46986aeb-b3ed-5a20-9bf3-78659d9de421" :question/id #uuid "46986aeb-b3ed-5a20-9bf3-78659d9de421" :question/math-academy-id "q-111174" :question/problem "![](images/04/04a4c0b720676f48d1587c2e8ff0cd7096868ef0192738812af09bba725fd224.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{4}f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "To graph the function $y=\\frac{1}{4}f(x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and compress it by factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nThe resulting graph is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/e7/e7f418df59b24e1410b172f362c087241b85c0fa9861231ec352f80cbc0668ff.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bdb4473c-84af-5e05-a80a-89f2a6a04705"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bdb4473c-84af-5e05-a80a-89f2a6a04705" :answer-field/id #uuid "bdb4473c-84af-5e05-a80a-89f2a6a04705" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d5cc25c3-1cb1-5454-bbd8-68f4535626b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47254958-c6e9-508c-ab38-416305b1b3df" "answer-6d1c33c6-4f01-51ce-906e-400e9a367abd" "answer-73a47950-119b-501c-b6d6-3dcaa1db8188" "answer-d5cc25c3-1cb1-5454-bbd8-68f4535626b4" "answer-6f2e6727-9491-5e81-abbf-30bc6689d940"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47254958-c6e9-508c-ab38-416305b1b3df" :answer/id #uuid "47254958-c6e9-508c-ab38-416305b1b3df" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/12/12d4221b81ac7e5b7d5215df9bcedcce32cad9296d43fac4f766