answer-field/choices 17592186067578] {:db/id 17592186068734 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d34958ec-5dd9-5a10-8bd6-7504a0d293c1" "question-1d4ef9d9-890a-5da6-8625-b613890df574" "question-1d5e523f-cb45-5cb6-96e4-37ea7521523c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068735 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-706f56b6-76a3-5149-b5e7-35082287eff9" "question-204edd9f-19f2-513e-ac33-9db65e721229"] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Indefinite Integral of an Exponential-Trigonometric Expression Using Integration by Parts" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068801 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-509669b5-ef46-5eb1-8d54-7bbaca5f8fc9" "question-0b786a85-3015-50d7-b6da-f38d91ed719a" "question-ce3e4235-61fa-5c48-8fde-1e9523a76255"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d34958ec-5dd9-5a10-8bd6-7504a0d293c1" :question/id #uuid "d34958ec-5dd9-5a10-8bd6-7504a0d293c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114951" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "First, we let\n\n$$\nI=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{8}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{8{ln}^{7}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{8}⁡x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(\\frac{8{ln}^{7}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{9}⁡x-8\\int \\frac{{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{9}⁡x-8I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $I,$ remembering to add a constant of integration $C$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{9}⁡x-8I \\\\ 9I & ={ln}^{9}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4338b54c-776e-5c97-9d8a-821ddad0e1e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4338b54c-776e-5c97-9d8a-821ddad0e1e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4338b54c-776e-5c97-9d8a-821ddad0e1e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7b7a4366-3be3-5b98-9a3e-ba4a656574ea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a44699f-24c8-5a58-ba2d-76fbbc86ccec" "answer-f5af7b76-5c7d-52a9-8262-1e2bfb500412" "answer-8e73f739-d875-5435-8483-802c12bd03ee" "answer-fc69b155-6de6-5e6d-a369-6a5bbeeb4817" "answer-7b7a4366-3be3-5b98-9a3e-ba4a656574ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a44699f-24c8-5a58-ba2d-76fbbc86ccec" :answer/id #uuid "5a44699f-24c8-5a58-ba2d-76fbbc86ccec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{7}⁡x}{3}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5af7b76-5c7d-52a9-8262-1e2bfb500412" :answer/id #uuid "f5af7b76-5c7d-52a9-8262-1e2bfb500412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{7}⁡x}{7}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e73f739-d875-5435-8483-802c12bd03ee" :answer/id #uuid "8e73f739-d875-5435-8483-802c12bd03ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{3}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc69b155-6de6-5e6d-a369-6a5bbeeb4817" :answer/id #uuid "fc69b155-6de6-5e6d-a369-6a5bbeeb4817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{6}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b7a4366-3be3-5b98-9a3e-ba4a656574ea" :answer/id #uuid "7b7a4366-3be3-5b98-9a3e-ba4a656574ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{9}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d4ef9d9-890a-5da6-8625-b613890df574" :question/id #uuid "1d4ef9d9-890a-5da6-8625-b613890df574" :question/math-academy-id "q-348879" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{6x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{6x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{6x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{4}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{ln}^{3}⁡x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{6x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{4}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{6})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{6})(\\frac{4{ln}^{3}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{6}-4\\int \\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{6}-4I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{6}-4I \\\\ 5I & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{6} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{6x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{30}({ln}^{5}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}({ln}^{5}⁡({e}^{3})-{ln}^{5}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}((3\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{5}-{0}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}({3}^{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1146e643-4cd0-54ef-a3e2-eff97703cea4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1146e643-4cd0-54ef-a3e2-eff97703cea4" :answer-field/id #uuid "1146e643-4cd0-54ef-a3e2-eff97703cea4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c033b7b5-f0bb-5912-ac93-d7393c96dac2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c033b7b5-f0bb-5912-ac93-d7393c96dac2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c033b7b5-f0bb-5912-ac93-d7393c96dac2" :answer/id #uuid "c033b7b5-f0bb-5912-ac93-d7393c96dac2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{81}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d5e523f-cb45-5cb6-96e4-37ea7521523c" :question/id #uuid "1d5e523f-cb45-5cb6-96e4-37ea7521523c" :question/math-academy-id "q-348848" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{5}}\\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{5}}\\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{4}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{ln}^{3}⁡x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{3x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{4}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3})(\\frac{4{ln}^{3}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{3}-4\\int \\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{3}-4I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{3}-4I \\\\ 5I & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{3} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{5}}\\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡x}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{15}({ln}^{5}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}({ln}^{5}⁡({e}^{5})-{ln}^{5}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}((5\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{5}-{0}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}({5}^{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{625}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3a039a4-2ad9-58c4-9de9-69c93ba57a90"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3a039a4-2ad9-58c4-9de9-69c93ba57a90" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a039a4-2ad9-58c4-9de9-69c93ba57a90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ff5d37fa-afb4-58b9-ac62-05838ab2df59" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff5d37fa-afb4-58b9-ac62-05838ab2df59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff5d37fa-afb4-58b9-ac62-05838ab2df59" :answer/id #uuid "ff5d37fa-afb4-58b9-ac62-05838ab2df59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{625}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069401 :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡z}{z}\\,\\text{d}z$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡z}{z}\\,\\text{d}z.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{3}⁡z\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}=\\frac{3{ln}^{2}⁡z}{z}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}z}=\\frac{1}{z}\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡z}{z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={ln}^{3}⁡z(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)(\\frac{3{ln}^{2}⁡z}{z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={ln}^{4}⁡z-3\\int \\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡z}{z}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{4}⁡z-3I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{4}⁡z-3I \\\\ 4I & ={ln}^{4}⁡z \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{4}⁡z}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡z}{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\frac{1}{4}({ln}^{4}⁡z){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({ln}^{4}⁡(e)-{ln}^{4}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186067576 :answer-field/correct 17592186067579 :answer-field/choices ["answer-1c227681-1e75-580c-a1f0-afa6524eba89"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c227681-1e75-580c-a1f0-afa6524eba89" :answer/id #uuid "1c227681-1e75-580c-a1f0-afa6524eba89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-706f56b6-76a3-5149-b5e7-35082287eff9" :question/id #uuid "706f56b6-76a3-5149-b5e7-35082287eff9" :question/math-academy-id "q-3402" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-J \\\\ I & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+I) \\\\ I & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-I \\\\ 2I & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7665ab87-9f58-54f0-86a0-f924247bce54"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7665ab87-9f58-54f0-86a0-f924247bce54" :answer-field/id #uuid "7665ab87-9f58-54f0-86a0-f924247bce54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fdbcaaaa-e8c2-5f47-afab-364c965f5b98" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64649790-f668-59d7-9c45-e3aba8bd1d38" "answer-a3428012-52f2-5611-af94-dbc2d0e4d7ee" "answer-8b6b83e9-8074-57f6-8288-2a2fc643233f" "answer-fdbcaaaa-e8c2-5f47-afab-364c965f5b98" "answer-2a1bf69d-6891-560f-b34a-b2a74af9646e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64649790-f668-59d7-9c45-e3aba8bd1d38" :answer/id #uuid "64649790-f668-59d7-9c45-e3aba8bd1d38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3428012-52f2-5611-af94-dbc2d0e4d7ee" :answer/id #uuid "a3428012-52f2-5611-af94-dbc2d0e4d7ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b6b83e9-8074-57f6-8288-2a2fc643233f" :answer/id #uuid "8b6b83e9-8074-57f6-8288-2a2fc643233f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdbcaaaa-e8c2-5f47-afab-364c965f5b98" :answer/id #uuid "fdbcaaaa-e8c2-5f47-afab-364c965f5b98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a1bf69d-6891-560f-b34a-b2a74af9646e" :answer/id #uuid "2a1bf69d-6891-560f-b34a-b2a74af9646e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-204edd9f-19f2-513e-ac33-9db65e721229" :question/id #uuid "204edd9f-19f2-513e-ac33-9db65e721229" :question/math-academy-id "q-12924" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}J \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}I \\\\ \\frac{10}{9}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9} \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{10}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a6ff2439-5d4f-5486-b23d-8199292dfe50"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a6ff2439-5d4f-5486-b23d-8199292dfe50" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6ff2439-5d4f-5486-b23d-8199292dfe50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2e5f1481-f060-5e2c-a1ba-9d650eb0364e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8abaac36-eba4-5279-995b-1ce237e32fb8" "answer-2e5f1481-f060-5e2c-a1ba-9d650eb0364e" "answer-6cede503-5875-5d7e-acae-646cdb24f91a" "answer-c80ff131-1ac8-5344-98c3-286bacff57ca" "answer-3de57636-1ffa-509b-8522-11db772f0631"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8abaac36-eba4-5279-995b-1ce237e32fb8" :answer/id #uuid "8abaac36-eba4-5279-995b-1ce237e32fb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{-x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{10}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e5f1481-f060-5e2c-a1ba-9d650eb0364e" :answer/id #uuid "2e5f1481-f060-5e2c-a1ba-9d650eb0364e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{10}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cede503-5875-5d7e-acae-646cdb24f91a" :answer/id #uuid "6cede503-5875-5d7e-acae-646cdb24f91a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{5}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c80ff131-1ac8-5344-98c3-286bacff57ca" :answer/id #uuid "c80ff131-1ac8-5344-98c3-286bacff57ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{5}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3de57636-1ffa-509b-8522-11db772f0631" :answer/id #uuid "3de57636-1ffa-509b-8522-11db772f0631" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{10}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-509669b5-ef46-5eb1-8d54-7bbaca5f8fc9" :question/id #uuid "509669b5-ef46-5eb1-8d54-7bbaca5f8fc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-115002" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}J \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}I) \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}I \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}I & =\\frac{2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})))-(\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-0}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0))-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(0)))) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi /2}}{5}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi /2}+1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2392f4ba-bd38-5a07-8e70-90353132c90f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2392f4ba-bd38-5a07-8e70-90353132c90f" :answer-field/id #uuid "2392f4ba-bd38-5a07-8e70-90353132c90f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8bff236b-251c-5407-acdf-108c7f7dd322" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c07201a8-c8e4-5b0a-831a-ee4bce670816" "answer-842dae31-aac6-5e10-b497-9abe5c499c5b" "answer-8bff236b-251c-5407-acdf-108c7f7dd322" "answer-6081e439-1860-5222-91b9-aee228c648b6" "answer-0ec2f68f-3a5c-5320-80df-4677e1be6e00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c07201a8-c8e4-5b0a-831a-ee4bce670816" :answer/id #uuid "c07201a8-c8e4-5b0a-831a-ee4bce670816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-\\pi /2}+1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-842dae31-aac6-5e10-b497-9abe5c499c5b" :answer/id #uuid "842dae31-aac6-5e10-b497-9abe5c499c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-\\pi /2}-1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bff236b-251c-5407-acdf-108c7f7dd322" :answer/id #uuid "8bff236b-251c-5407-acdf-108c7f7dd322" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi /2}+1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6081e439-1860-5222-91b9-aee228c648b6" :answer/id #uuid "6081e439-1860-5222-91b9-aee228c648b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }+2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ec2f68f-3a5c-5320-80df-4677e1be6e00" :answer/id #uuid "0ec2f68f-3a5c-5320-80df-4677e1be6e00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }-1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0b786a85-3015-50d7-b6da-f38d91ed719a" :question/id #uuid "0b786a85-3015-50d7-b6da-f38d91ed719a" :question/math-academy-id "q-115003" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2J \\\\ I & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2(-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2I) \\\\ I & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4I \\\\ 5I & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{-2\\pi /2}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})))-(\\frac{{e}^{-2(0)}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{5}+\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{-\\pi }+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2abcc4ca-4f5a-5ee4-b3d4-9f4549d9ca5d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2abcc4ca-4f5a-5ee4-b3d4-9f4549d9ca5d" :answer-field/id #uuid "2abcc4ca-4f5a-5ee4-b3d4-9f4549d9ca5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-99e7c620-6fc1-5713-836c-454ba4907213" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b036bbd1-1c23-5d6d-9a9d-9e351a182b4e" "answer-0340ba7d-60fe-5ce5-94fe-c3642864b856" "answer-6d3d7672-ea17-5f1b-946d-cbc34bf9be65" "answer-99e7c620-6fc1-5713-836c-454ba4907213" "answer-200d0628-556e-5baa-ac44-a3d113c85b7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b036bbd1-1c23-5d6d-9a9d-9e351a182b4e" :answer/id #uuid "b036bbd1-1c23-5d6d-9a9d-9e351a182b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}({e}^{-2\\pi }+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0340ba7d-60fe-5ce5-94fe-c3642864b856" :answer/id #uuid "0340ba7d-60fe-5ce5-94fe-c3642864b856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}({e}^{-\\pi }-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d3d7672-ea17-5f1b-946d-cbc34bf9be65" :answer/id #uuid "6d3d7672-ea17-5f1b-946d-cbc34bf9be65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{-2\\pi }-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99e7c620-6fc1-5713-836c-454ba4907213" :answer/id #uuid "99e7c620-6fc1-5713-836c-454ba4907213" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{-\\pi }+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-200d0628-556e-5baa-ac44-a3d113c85b7f" :answer/id #uuid "200d0628-556e-5baa-ac44-a3d113c85b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{-\\pi }-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186323217 :answer-field/correct "answer-cde87829-8161-59e8-a5a9-817dbc346072" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cde87829-8161-59e8-a5a9-817dbc346072"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cde87829-8161-59e8-a5a9-817dbc346072" :answer/id #uuid "cde87829-8161-59e8-a5a9-817dbc346072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-\\pi}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ce3e4235-61fa-5c48-8fde-1e9523a76255" :question/id #uuid "ce3e4235-61fa-5c48-8fde-1e9523a76255" :question/math-academy-id "q-115005" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+J \\\\ I & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-I) \\\\ I & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-I \\\\ 2I & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ))-(\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }-{e}^{\\pi }}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-feba3f58-6495-56d8-aeb6-29990aa6bdd2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-feba3f58-6495-56d8-aeb6-29990aa6bdd2" :answer-field/id #uuid "feba3f58-6495-56d8-aeb6-29990aa6bdd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4a9bb87c-c499-5aa9-adb7-e327fbd1e96b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-02e5024b-1c1c-54cb-83fb-120b748a9ccc" "answer-423c048e-ea22-5f3a-ad4f-122dccb7ad0d" "answer-4a9bb87c-c499-5aa9-adb7-e327fbd1e96b" "answer-d48a3ee5-6a7b-5611-a42f-6f64ee2d3a9a" "answer-9e2c4c31-6263-5a76-9ab5-f8cd0d8c8d92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02e5024b-1c1c-54cb-83fb-120b748a9ccc" :answer/id #uuid "02e5024b-1c1c-54cb-83fb-120b748a9ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }+2{e}^{\\pi }}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-423c048e-ea22-5f3a-ad4f-122dccb7ad0d" :answer/id #uuid "423c048e-ea22-5f3a-ad4f-122dccb7ad0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{-2\\pi }}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a9bb87c-c499-5aa9-adb7-e327fbd1e96b" :answer/id #uuid "4a9bb87c-c499-5aa9-adb7-e327fbd1e96b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }-{e}^{\\pi }}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d48a3ee5-6a7b-5611-a42f-6f64ee2d3a9a" :answer/id #uuid "d48a3ee5-6a7b-5611-a42f-6f64ee2d3a9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2\\pi }-1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e2c4c31-6263-5a76-9ab5-f8cd0d8c8d92" :answer/id #uuid "9e2c4c31-6263-5a76-9ab5-f8cd0d8c8d92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }+{e}^{-\\pi }}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070032 :tutorial/content "In some cases, applying integration by parts can lead to a cyclic pattern, where the original integral reappears after a few steps. This cyclic behavior allows us to solve the integral by forming an equation that can be solved algebraically.\n\nTo illustrate, let's consider the following example:\n\n$$\nI = \\int \\dfrac{\\ln x}{x} \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nLet's try using the method of integration by parts. We suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡x-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡x-I\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have the same integral $I$ on both sides of the equality. Thinking about $I$ as some unknown variable, we can easily solve this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{2}⁡x-I \\\\ I+I & ={ln}^{2}⁡x \\\\ 2I & ={ln}^{2}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we added a constant of integration right at the very end of the calculation." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068957 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069630 :step/math-academy-id 640946 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069631 :step/math-academy-id 640947 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069632 :step/math-academy-id 640950 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069725 :step/math-academy-id 640953 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e707f526-b15a-5f98-b415-f7cf137b340a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e707f526-b15a-5f98-b415-f7cf137b340a" :question/id #uuid "e707f526-b15a-5f98-b415-f7cf137b340a" :question/math-academy-id "q-146207" :question/problem "| $y$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ | $0.35$ | $0.65$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=3.3.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.35+(4)^{2}\\cdot 0.65]-{(3.3)}^{2} \\\\  & =1.4+10.4-10.89 \\\\  & =0.91.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-16d85871-d920-5dbd-a4cd-98b30b38c426"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-16d85871-d920-5dbd-a4cd-98b30b38c426" :answer-field/id #uuid "16d85871-d920-5dbd-a4cd-98b30b38c426" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-01d541fc-140e-5f1b-bba5-29b574f9aba1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c0bc7df8-3240-5054-a55e-249b2d539736" "answer-31c8f999-6313-5508-98ec-8bfe6a704e41" "answer-01d541fc-140e-5f1b-bba5-29b574f9aba1" "answer-c2e8b4fb-c38c-501f-9b11-c569642015ff" "answer-049f6a2f-a547-5ec8-9a37-c46281090582"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0bc7df8-3240-5054-a55e-249b2d539736" :answer/id #uuid "c0bc7df8-3240-5054-a55e-249b2d539736" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.58" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31c8f999-6313-5508-98ec-8bfe6a704e41" :answer/id #uuid "31c8f999-6313-5508-98ec-8bfe6a704e41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01d541fc-140e-5f1b-bba5-29b574f9aba1" :answer/id #uuid "01d541fc-140e-5f1b-bba5-29b574f9aba1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.91" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2e8b4fb-c38c-501f-9b11-c569642015ff" :answer/id #uuid "c2e8b4fb-c38c-501f-9b11-c569642015ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.02" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-049f6a2f-a547-5ec8-9a37-c46281090582" :answer/id #uuid "049f6a2f-a547-5ec8-9a37-c46281090582" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188328 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b82a91db-40b3-51bf-b539-d94cf7913732"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b82a91db-40b3-51bf-b539-d94cf7913732" :question/id #uuid "b82a91db-40b3-51bf-b539-d94cf7913732" :question/math-academy-id "q-146284" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)]-{\\mu }_{X|4}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}]-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-caa5996b-3602-50fb-816f-2fafeaae3fc0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-caa5996b-3602-50fb-816f-2fafeaae3fc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "caa5996b-3602-50fb-816f-2fafeaae3fc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6771ee98-f25a-5cdc-91d7-e1d71d8eda3c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b01056a8-96d8-5259-85d4-db47041ed857" "answer-5dbc9f32-3c2a-5c31-81b2-2d34ba3625e9" "answer-83542680-0c0f-5bce-90df-2f3546c7a3e2" "answer-3c5745e4-3ad7-502f-bce7-234772762acf" "answer-6771ee98-f25a-5cdc-91d7-e1d71d8eda3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b01056a8-96d8-5259-85d4-db47041ed857" :answer/id #uuid "b01056a8-96d8-5259-85d4-db47041ed857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5dbc9f32-3c2a-5c31-81b2-2d34ba3625e9" :answer/id #uuid "5dbc9f32-3c2a-5c31-81b2-2d34ba3625e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83542680-0c0f-5bce-90df-2f3546c7a3e2" :answer/id #uuid "83542680-0c0f-5bce-90df-2f3546c7a3e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c5745e4-3ad7-502f-bce7-234772762acf" :answer/id #uuid "3c5745e4-3ad7-502f-bce7-234772762acf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6771ee98-f25a-5cdc-91d7-e1d71d8eda3c" :answer/id #uuid "6771ee98-f25a-5cdc-91d7-e1d71d8eda3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-0de42b93-b491-50b2-9b2e-2548c7cf7804" :activity/id #uuid "0de42b93-b491-50b2-9b2e-2548c7cf7804" :activity/title "Conditional Variance for Discrete Random Variables" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049871 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-c8a3756c-04e8-556f-9cc2-eccde7fa83d2" "step-c91da45b-8d0d-5c23-88c6-ad0898a0b0e9" "step-dd392e09-3b07-5d93-9c6a-5ad2b4c1303f" "step-cdab31e1-2709-5be5-8924-bd47c546b80d" "step-cde0433b-a43b-5914-bcdd-1ad814f4d75a"] :activity/first-step "step-c8a3756c-04e8-556f-9cc2-eccde7fa83d2" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-c8a3756c-04e8-556f-9cc2-eccde7fa83d2" :step/id #uuid "c8a3756c-04e8-556f-9cc2-eccde7fa83d2" :step/content "question-e707f526-b15a-5f98-b415-f7cf137b340a" :step/next "step-c91da45b-8d0d-5c23-88c6-ad0898a0b0e9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c91da45b-8d0d-5c23-88c6-ad0898a0b0e9" :step/id #uuid "c91da45b-8d0d-5c23-88c6-ad0898a0b0e9" :step/content 17592186542228 :step/next "step-dd392e09-3b07-5d93-9c6a-5ad2b4c1303f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dd392e09-3b07-5d93-9c6a-5ad2b4c1303f" :step/id #uuid "dd392e09-3b07-5d93-9c6a-5ad2b4c1303f" :step/content 17592186188687 :step/next "step-cdab31e1-2709-5be5-8924-bd47c546b80d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cdab31e1-2709-5be5-8924-bd47c546b80d" :step/id #uuid "cdab31e1-2709-5be5-8924-bd47c546b80d" :step/content "question-b82a91db-40b3-51bf-b539-d94cf7913732" :step/next "step-cde0433b-a43b-5914-bcdd-1ad814f4d75a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cde0433b-a43b-5914-bcdd-1ad814f4d75a" :step/id #uuid "cde0433b-a43b-5914-bcdd-1ad814f4d75a" :step/content 17592186542174 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115200 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6adee969-6d90-563b-a4ef-2a55fc2a8432"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115219 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-49bb96bd-7826-5c22-b9da-330c6f2a3a6b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6adee969-6d90-563b-a4ef-2a55fc2a8432" :question/id #uuid "6adee969-6d90-563b-a4ef-2a55fc2a8432" :question/math-academy-id "q-26373" :question/problem "Find the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${27}^{x+2}={3}^{4x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base.\n\nTo do this, we write $27$ as ${3}^{3},$ and then rewrite the left-hand side using the power rule of exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{27}^{x+2} & ={3}^{4x} \\\\ {({3}^{3})}^{x+2} & ={3}^{4x} \\\\ {3}^{3(x+2)} & ={3}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(3)$, we equate the exponents and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+2) & =4x \\\\ 3x+6 & =4x \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d7feacf0-2600-5627-831e-b74ae6dc5e57"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d7feacf0-2600-5627-831e-b74ae6dc5e57" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7feacf0-2600-5627-831e-b74ae6dc5e57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-38bb578d-a62c-5025-bfe6-bf3bf4e7b8fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a6029de-df2f-54fb-a0ad-7d3957057ce0" "answer-79e4caac-dabc-5759-83c5-b05a28ec26a4" "answer-4125969d-9fb6-507b-aedc-9e29716ac69b" "answer-7a171f95-c8dd-5fcd-963f-a70b75e57103" "answer-38bb578d-a62c-5025-bfe6-bf3bf4e7b8fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a6029de-df2f-54fb-a0ad-7d3957057ce0" :answer/id #uuid "2a6029de-df2f-54fb-a0ad-7d3957057ce0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79e4caac-dabc-5759-83c5-b05a28ec26a4" :answer/id #uuid "79e4caac-dabc-5759-83c5-b05a28ec26a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4125969d-9fb6-507b-aedc-9e29716ac69b" :answer/id #uuid "4125969d-9fb6-507b-aedc-9e29716ac69b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a171f95-c8dd-5fcd-963f-a70b75e57103" :answer/id #uuid "7a171f95-c8dd-5fcd-963f-a70b75e57103" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38bb578d-a62c-5025-bfe6-bf3bf4e7b8fd" :answer/id #uuid "38bb578d-a62c-5025-bfe6-bf3bf4e7b8fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-49bb96bd-7826-5c22-b9da-330c6f2a3a6b" :question/id #uuid "49bb96bd-7826-5c22-b9da-330c6f2a3a6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-66881" :question/problem "Solve for $y$ where ${9}^{y}={27}^{y-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base. To do this, we rewrite the equation using $9={3}^{2}$ and $27={3}^{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{({3}^{2})}^{y}={({3}^{3})}^{y-3}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule of exponents. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2y}={3}^{3(y-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(3)$, we equate the exponents and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =3(y-3) \\\\ 2y & =3y-9 \\\\ y & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6e10a49-5bb8-53f2-b412-c67176d7bbe6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6e10a49-5bb8-53f2-b412-c67176d7bbe6" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6e10a49-5bb8-53f2-b412-c67176d7bbe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0c4937f2-8f12-51c8-ae53-f769c39220a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8352ea78-64b9-59b0-bf3b-06a01355ac4a" "answer-fe1ff9f1-ff9b-5864-b028-4c33077c8097" "answer-1f15fc78-39ea-5695-a24d-e245860cc751" "answer-1b8692c4-fb80-5af4-8a70-4bcdd2906eb6" "answer-0c4937f2-8f12-51c8-ae53-f769c39220a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8352ea78-64b9-59b0-bf3b-06a01355ac4a" :answer/id #uuid "8352ea78-64b9-59b0-bf3b-06a01355ac4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe1ff9f1-ff9b-5864-b028-4c33077c8097" :answer/id #uuid "fe1ff9f1-ff9b-5864-b028-4c33077c8097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f15fc78-39ea-5695-a24d-e245860cc751" :answer/id #uuid "1f15fc78-39ea-5695-a24d-e245860cc751" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b8692c4-fb80-5af4-8a70-4bcdd2906eb6" :answer/id #uuid "1b8692c4-fb80-5af4-8a70-4bcdd2906eb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c4937f2-8f12-51c8-ae53-f769c39220a7" :answer/id #uuid "0c4937f2-8f12-51c8-ae53-f769c39220a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115417 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221987 :question/problem "The local truncation error (LTE) of a numerical method with step size $Δx$ is\n\n$$\nτ(Δx)=7(Δx)^{4}-2(Δx)^{5}.\n$$\n\nComplete the following sentences.\n\n$\\,$ With step size $Δx=0.5,$ the local truncation error is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ With step size $Δx=0.25,$ the local truncation error is $≈$\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Decreasing from $Δx=0.5$ to $Δx=0.25,$ the LTE is reduced by a factor of $≈$\n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ According to this data, the order of the method is approximately\n{{field-4}}." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6b9c9bd1-2a87-5558-b9d0-2d6b63e5b4ff" :activity/id #uuid "6b9c9bd1-2a87-5558-b9d0-2d6b63e5b4ff" :activity/title "Order of Numerical Methods" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051034 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-d6ec6828-2a53-5413-abf8-e2551fe3c1a1" "step-08502507-c59a-5867-999a-ebba7f4087e6" "step-62263311-e4e4-5c27-9f63-344d10ef049c" "step-6fb36135-f6fa-588f-a4ab-175dcddd7350" "step-73fce120-ef70-569c-9cac-599dfcb9f9ed"] :activity/first-step "step-d6ec6828-2a53-5413-abf8-e2551fe3c1a1" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d6ec6828-2a53-5413-abf8-e2551fe3c1a1" :step/id #uuid "d6ec6828-2a53-5413-abf8-e2551fe3c1a1" :step/content 17592186308493 :step/next "step-08502507-c59a-5867-999a-ebba7f4087e6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-08502507-c59a-5867-999a-ebba7f4087e6" :step/id #uuid "08502507-c59a-5867-999a-ebba7f4087e6" :step/content 17592186221987 :step/next "step-62263311-e4e4-5c27-9f63-344d10ef049c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-62263311-e4e4-5c27-9f63-344d10ef049c" :step/id #uuid "62263311-e4e4-5c27-9f63-344d10ef049c" :step/content 17592186443229 :step/next "step-6fb36135-f6fa-588f-a4ab-175dcddd7350" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6fb36135-f6fa-588f-a4ab-175dcddd7350" :step/id #uuid "6fb36135-f6fa-588f-a4ab-175dcddd7350" :step/content 17592186308680 :step/next "step-73fce120-ef70-569c-9cac-599dfcb9f9ed" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-73fce120-ef70-569c-9cac-599dfcb9f9ed" :step/id #uuid "73fce120-ef70-569c-9cac-599dfcb9f9ed" :step/content 17592186308686 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110615 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6679348c-4b94-5c71-ad1e-c5e2e39219c8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6679348c-4b94-5c71-ad1e-c5e2e39219c8" :question/id #uuid "6679348c-4b94-5c71-ad1e-c5e2e39219c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-23909" :question/problem "Consider the equation ${x}^{2}+1=k.$ For which values of $k$ does this equation have no real solutions?" :question/worked-solution "Let's try and solve using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+1 & =k \\\\ {x}^{2} & =k-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{k-1} \\\\ |x| & =\\sqrt{k-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation will have no real solutions if the expression under the square root is negative, which gives the following condition:\n\n$$\nk-1<0\n$$\n\nWe solve this inequality for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k-1 & <0 \\\\ k & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, any value of $k$ that is less than $1$ will give an equation with no real solutions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d66ee932-5e98-5dcc-a364-81a8f8aab903"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d66ee932-5e98-5dcc-a364-81a8f8aab903" :answer-field/id #uuid "d66ee932-5e98-5dcc-a364-81a8f8aab903" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8cfc645a-d731-58d6-b481-e809bbf004c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-62cb63a8-19e0-588e-9db0-dfaecf1c5151" "answer-8cfc645a-d731-58d6-b481-e809bbf004c2" "answer-2fa5fc1e-a0f6-5966-bb74-7c7870f75585" "answer-9af04c2f-bbcb-574d-aea2-43165947b74d" "answer-a19aba6e-b8ff-5e28-ac1a-a1f4ccb147c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62cb63a8-19e0-588e-9db0-dfaecf1c5151" :answer/id #uuid "62cb63a8-19e0-588e-9db0-dfaecf1c5151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cfc645a-d731-58d6-b481-e809bbf004c2" :answer/id #uuid "8cfc645a-d731-58d6-b481-e809bbf004c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k<1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fa5fc1e-a0f6-5966-bb74-7c7870f75585" :answer/id #uuid "2fa5fc1e-a0f6-5966-bb74-7c7870f75585" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k>-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9af04c2f-bbcb-574d-aea2-43165947b74d" :answer/id #uuid "9af04c2f-bbcb-574d-aea2-43165947b74d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k>1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a19aba6e-b8ff-5e28-ac1a-a1f4ccb147c7" :answer/id #uuid "a19aba6e-b8ff-5e28-ac1a-a1f4ccb147c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110614 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e09c7bc1-cc56-5292-bdc6-0155dadb5e01"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e09c7bc1-cc56-5292-bdc6-0155dadb5e01" :question/id #uuid "e09c7bc1-cc56-5292-bdc6-0155dadb5e01" :question/math-academy-id "q-52265" :question/problem "Given that  $64-64w+16{w}^{2}=0$, find $w.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the left-hand side is a perfect square. It just needs to be factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64-64w+16{w}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {8}^{2}-2\\cdot 8\\cdot 4w+(4w)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (8-4w)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(8-4w)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |8-4w| & =0 \\\\ 8-4w & =0 \\\\ 4w & =8 \\\\ w & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34420ca9-d74d-5ceb-bb68-1f1b54c6ad1f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34420ca9-d74d-5ceb-bb68-1f1b54c6ad1f" :answer-field/id #uuid "34420ca9-d74d-5ceb-bb68-1f1b54c6ad1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b00e279b-684b-51a7-94af-527772a83d48" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b00e279b-684b-51a7-94af-527772a83d48" "answer-4d80400f-b2d0-54b9-9ed3-e5ecca731644" "answer-aa279c53-f443-593f-af08-6cc45f50bcb3" "answer-048d8ec8-9ca8-5505-93f8-840a311956fe" "answer-475a999b-2d7e-58d1-898b-b645cc60c183"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b00e279b-684b-51a7-94af-527772a83d48" :answer/id #uuid "b00e279b-684b-51a7-94af-527772a83d48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d80400f-b2d0-54b9-9ed3-e5ecca731644" :answer/id #uuid "4d80400f-b2d0-54b9-9ed3-e5ecca731644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=2,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa279c53-f443-593f-af08-6cc45f50bcb3" :answer/id #uuid "aa279c53-f443-593f-af08-6cc45f50bcb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-048d8ec8-9ca8-5505-93f8-840a311956fe" :answer/id #uuid "048d8ec8-9ca8-5505-93f8-840a311956fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "w=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-475a999b-2d7e-58d1-898b-b645cc60c183" :answer/id #uuid "475a999b-2d7e-58d1-898b-b645cc60c183" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No real solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110613 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d0ec07f9-1330-5f73-b5fc-18b90684baa7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d0ec07f9-1330-5f73-b5fc-18b90684baa7" :question/id #uuid "d0ec07f9-1330-5f73-b5fc-18b90684baa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-222414" :question/problem "Which value of $h$ gives precisely one solution to the equation ${x}^{2}-h=2?$\n\n$h=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-h & =2 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =2+h \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{2+h} \\\\ |x| & =\\sqrt{2+h}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has only one solution if the right-hand side is equal to zero, and the right-hand side is zero only if the expression underneath the radical is zero. So, we solve for the value of $h$ that makes the expression under the radical equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+h & =0 \\\\ h & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $h=-2$ will give only one solution to the equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-908ab81d-c6d9-5ff9-acb5-ec458e5404d7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-908ab81d-c6d9-5ff9-acb5-ec458e5404d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "908ab81d-c6d9-5ff9-acb5-ec458e5404d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4a928ab0-ab65-547b-a92d-a3572e570e71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a928ab0-ab65-547b-a92d-a3572e570e71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a928ab0-ab65-547b-a92d-a3572e570e71" :answer/id #uuid "4a928ab0-ab65-547b-a92d-a3572e570e71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f093369d-b14e-5869-aee8-2e6ce5540050" :activity/id #uuid "f093369d-b14e-5869-aee8-2e6ce5540050" :activity/title "Perfect Square Quadratic Equations with One or No Solutions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049668 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-a323b5f9-d32e-52fb-ba12-a1996673427b" "step-d818973d-772d-5615-9419-e6057af17ee9" "step-6cb7afce-9837-5cfe-8b86-1ee68f54c9e3"] :activity/first-step "step-a323b5f9-d32e-52fb-ba12-a1996673427b" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-a323b5f9-d32e-52fb-ba12-a1996673427b" :step/id #uuid "a323b5f9-d32e-52fb-ba12-a1996673427b" :step/content "question-6679348c-4b94-5c71-ad1e-c5e2e39219c8" :step/next "step-d818973d-772d-5615-9419-e6057af17ee9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d818973d-772d-5615-9419-e6057af17ee9" :step/id #uuid "d818973d-772d-5615-9419-e6057af17ee9" :step/content "question-e09c7bc1-cc56-5292-bdc6-0155dadb5e01" :step/next "step-6cb7afce-9837-5cfe-8b86-1ee68f54c9e3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 